<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<gpx version="1.1" creator="Good Shit" xmlns="http://www.topografix.com/GPX/1/1"><trk><name>Kumano Kodo: Hosshinmon-oji to Hongu — Kumano Kodo: Hosshinmon-oji to Hongu</name><desc>The Hosshinmon-oji–Hongu walk follows the final section of the Kumano Kodo’s Nakahechi pilgrimage trail in Wakayama. Forest paths alternate with small villages, tea fields and stone steps before arriving at Kumano Hongu Taisha through its quieter rear approach. The route is mostly downhill, with some short climbs and uneven ground. Allow about three walking hours plus time at the shrine. Take the bus to the start and check the return timetable before setting out.

